                  %mi λ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  PGL_2(k)
                  \\coloneqq
                  GL_2(k)/\{\lambda I: \lambda \in k^\times\}
                  \\,.
          %p
            If, as in the case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{C}
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"}> complex numbers
            ), each element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^\times
            has a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+root"} square root
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+special+linear+group"} projective special linear group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi SL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ±
                  %mi I
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  PSL_2(k)
                  \\coloneqq
                  SL_2(k)/\pm I
                  \\,.
          %p
            Alternatively, a fractional linear transformation can be considered as synonymous with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+functions"} rational functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k(x)
            as a field over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transcendence+degree"} transcendence degree
            1.
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analysis"} complex analysis
            (which is the usual context when one speaks of Möbius transformations; otherwise one usually calls them by some combination of “linear” and “fractional”), Möbius transformations are precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biholomorphisms"} biholomorphisms
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijective
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+transformations"} conformal transformations
          %p
            Often, and particularly when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is the the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+group"} modular group
            where the coefficients
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, b, c, d
            are assumed to lie in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+domain"} integral domain
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mi b
                    %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a d - b c = 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+half-plane"} upper half-plane
            by the group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PGL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PGL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
            over the
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#crossratios Cross-ratios
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The action
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PGL
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PGL_2(k) \times \mathbb{P}^1(k) \to \mathbb{P}^1(k)
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+action"} 3-transitive
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a, b, c)
              may be mapped to any other triplet of distinct points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a', b', c')
              by applying a group element.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              It suffices to consider
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a' = 0, b' = 1, c' = \infty
              where one applies the transformation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ↦
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo −
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi b
                          %mo −
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo −
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi b
                          %mo −
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto \frac{(x-a)(b-c)}{(x-c)(b-a)}
          %p
            This motivates the following definition: given a 4-tuple
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a, b, c, d)
            of distinct points in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}^1(k)
            %em cross-ratio
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma(a, b, c, d) = \frac{(d-a)(b-c)}{(d-c)(b-a)}.
          %p
            It is not hard to see that the group action preserves the cross-ratio, i.e.,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma(g \cdot a, g \cdot b, g \cdot c, g \cdot d) = \gamma(a, b, c, d)
          %p
            In the case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{C}
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℙ
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}^1
            is interpreted as the Riemann sphere, it turns out that the cross-ratio of a 4-tuple is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            if and only if the four points lie on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            (or a line which is a circle passing through
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %h3#action_on_hyperbolic_space Action on hyperbolic space
          %p
            As explained at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincare+group"} Poincare group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSL_2(\mathbb{C})
            can be identified with those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+transformations"} linear transformations
            of Minkowski space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^4
            that preserve the Minkowski
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+form"} form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            = succeed "-preserving," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light+cone"} light cone
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi v
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{v = (\vec{x}, t): Q(v) = 0, t \gt 0\}
            to itself. It follows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSL_2(\mathbb{C})
            acts on the hyperboloid sheet
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi v
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^3 = \{v = (\vec{x}, t): Q(v) = 1, t \gt 0\}
          %p
            which is naturally identified with hyperbolic 3-space. There is a Poincaré disk model for
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^3
            that is the intersection of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/future+cone"} future cone
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi v
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{v = (\vec{x}, t): Q(v) \geq 0, t \gt 0\}
            with the hyperplane
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi int
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} int(D^3)
            which can be placed in perspective with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^3
            by considering lines through the origin in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^4
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^3
            passes through a unique point of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi int
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} int(D^3)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^3
            is viewed as a natural compactification of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSL_2(\mathbb{C})
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^3
            induces an action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSL_2(\mathbb{C})
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∂
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2 = \partial D^3
            (“the heavenly sphere”) coincides with the action on the Riemann sphere
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2 = \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{C})
          %h2#ModularGroup Modular group
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+group"} modular group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            is the subgroup
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi PSL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSL_2(\mathbb{Z}) \hookrightarrow PSL_2(\mathbb{C})
            consisting of Möbius transformations with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                  %mo ↦
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi z
                      %mo +
                      %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mi z
                      %mo +
                      %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \mapsto \frac{a z + b}{c z + d}
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, b, c, d \in \mathbb{Z}
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mi b
                    %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a d - b c = 1
          %p
            The group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSL_2(\mathbb{R})
            acts on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+half-plane"} upper half-plane
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi z
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H = \{z \in \mathbb{C}: Im(z) \geq 0\}
            (or rather
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \cup \{\infty\}
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
            of the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSL_2(\mathbb{C})
            on the Riemann sphere. Indeed, the action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSL_2(\mathbb{R})
            takes the real line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \cup \{\infty\}
            to itself, and any element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi z
                      %mo +
                      %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mi z
                      %mo +
                      %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(z) = \frac{a z + b}{c z + d}
            takes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo +
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mi c
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi d
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b + a i)(d - c i)/(c^2 + d^2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ad
                  %mo −
                  %mi b
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (ad - b c)/(c^2 + d^2) = 1/(c^2 + d^2)
            is positive. By continuity it follows that the action preserves the sign of the imaginary part, hence takes the upper-half plane
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            to itself.
          %p
            It is illuminating to think of complex numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Im(\tau) \gt 0
            as representing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves"} elliptic curves
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meromorphic+functions"} meromorphic functions
            on an elliptic curve (i.e., a complex projective curve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus"} genus
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            equipped with a structure of complex analytic 1-manifold) can be identified with a field of doubly periodic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+functions"} holomorphic functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi L
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℙ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}/L \to \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{C})
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L = \langle \omega_1, \omega_2\rangle
            is a fundamental lattice (a discrete cocompact subgroup of the additive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weierstrass+elliptic+functions"} Weierstrass elliptic functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℘
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi L
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℙ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wp(z), \wp'(z): \mathbb{C}/L \to \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{C})
            (here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℘
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wp'
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative"} derivative
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wp
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubic+curve"} cubic algebraic relation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℘
                  %mo ′
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mn 4
                  %msup
                    %mi ℘
                    %mn 3
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                  %mi ℘
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\wp')^2 = 4\wp^3 - g_2\wp - g_3
          %p
            where the constants
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_2, g_3
            are expressed as certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eisenstein+series"} Eisenstein series
            in the fundamental periods
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1, \omega_2
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
            elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1, \omega_2
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
            may be arranged so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau = \omega_2/\omega_1
            has positive imaginary part. Of course, if there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homothety"} homothety
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi λ
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \mapsto \lambda z
            that takes a lattice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            to a lattice
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L'
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = \mathbb{C}/L
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi L
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E' = \mathbb{C}/L'
            are analytically isomorphic, so the map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau \mapsto \mathbb{C}/\langle 1, \tau\rangle
          %p
            gives a surjection from complex numbers with positive imaginary part to isomorphism classes of smooth elliptic curves. Thus we may restrict attention to lattices of the form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L = \langle 1, \tau \rangle
          %p
            Of course,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            admits more than one such basis
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1, \tau)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1, \tau')
            there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+transformation"} linear transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi PSL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \in \Gamma \coloneqq PSL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi τ
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma(\tau) = \tau'
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+space"} orbit space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi τ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\tau \in \mathbb{C}: Im(\tau) \gt 0\}/\Gamma
          %p
            is a coarse
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            for elliptic curves. In this context, one often says that elliptic curves are paramatrized by the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/j-invariant"} invariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+form"} modular form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(\tau)
            defined on the upper half-plane such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(\tau) = j(\tau')
            if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %mi γ
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau' = \gamma \cdot \tau
            for some
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \in \Gamma
          %p
            Of course, in some cases there may be more than one
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \in \Gamma
            that fixes a given
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            is a fourth root of unity or a sixth root of unity. A more refined approach then is to consider, instead of the coarse orbit space, the (compactified)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (H \cup \{\infty\})//\Gamma
            for elliptic curves, as a central geometric object of interest.
          %h3#abstract_structure_of_modular_group Abstract structure of modular group
          %p
            As an abstract
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi PSL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma = PSL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+product"} free product
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/(2) \ast \mathbb{Z}/(3)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            to be given by the Moebius transformation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \mapsto -1/z
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            to be given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \mapsto (z-1)/z
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+group"} concrete group
            and certain of its subgroups, such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence+subgroups"} congruence subgroups
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/continued+fraction#rational_tangles"} rational tangles
            and of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+map"} trivalent maps
          %p
            It is also worth pointing out that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            is a quotient of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+group"} braid group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_3
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_3
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_2
            subject to the relation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_1 \sigma_2 \sigma_1 = \sigma_2 \sigma_1 \sigma_2.
          %p
            Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \coloneqq (\sigma_1 \sigma_2)^3
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/center"} central element
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_3
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi z
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 3
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi q
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \to \mathbb{Z} \stackrel{1 \mapsto z}{\to} B_3 \stackrel{q}{\to} \Gamma \to 1
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            is the unique homomorphism mapping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_1\sigma_2
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mi z
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda z. (z-1)/z
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_1\sigma_2\sigma_1
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mi z
                    %mo .
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                      %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda z. \frac{-1}{z}
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SL%282%2CZ%29"} SL(2,Z)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+group"} conformal group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleinian+group"} Kleinian group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence+subgroup"} congruence subgroup
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+n+subgroup"}> level n subgroup
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} modular equivariant elliptic cohomology
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Named after
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/August+M%C3%B6bius"} August Möbius
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Pierre+Serre"}> Jean-Pierre Serre
              , §VII.1 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Course in Arithmetic
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 7
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4684-9884-4"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4684-9884-4
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.purdue.edu/~jlipman/MA598/Serre-Course%20in%20Arithmetic.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Projective_linear_group"} Projective linear group
